---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, ISSUES_URL, RELEASES_REPO, SOURCE_URL } from "../data/site";

const contact = CONTACT_EMAIL
  ? `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=${encodeURIComponent("Privacy")}`
  : ISSUES_URL;
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy: AGENCY OS"
  description="This website has no trackers, analytics or cookies. AGENCY OS keeps camera video on your Mac and memory under your control."
  current="privacy"
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p>
    <h1>Privacy, in plain words</h1>
    <p class="lede">Two parts: this website, and the AGENCY OS app.</p>

    <h2 id="site">This website</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No trackers, no analytics, no advertising, no cookies.</strong>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Fonts and files come from this site.</strong> Nothing is loaded from font services or other
        companies.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>One request to GitHub.</strong> To show the newest download, your browser asks GitHub's public
        API about the latest release of {RELEASES_REPO}. GitHub sees that request like any visit (including
        your IP address) under{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub's privacy statement
        </a>
        . The download itself also comes from GitHub. We don't receive anything about you from it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your theme choice stays in your browser.</strong> If you switch between light and dark, that
        choice is saved in your browser's local storage on your device. It's never sent anywhere. Clearing
        your browsing data removes it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Which Mac you have stays in your browser.</strong> The page checks your browser's information
        to suggest the Apple silicon or Intel download. That check happens on your device and isn't stored or
        sent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may keep server logs as described
        in its privacy statement. We don't have access to visitor logs and don't ask for them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="app">The AGENCY OS app</h2>
    <p>
      These are the rules AGENCY OS is built to follow. They are part of the project's safety rules, and every
      part of the app is built and tested against them.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera video never leaves your Mac.</strong> Frames are processed on the Mac to follow your
        eyes, then thrown away. They're never stored, and never sent to the AI or anywhere else. Your
        eye calibration is saved on the device as numbers, not pictures or video.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The AI sees only what a task needs, only when you start one.</strong> During a task you
        started, AGENCY may send Google's Gemini your request and screenshots of the app it's working in.
        Screenshots aren't kept by default. Google's terms apply to what's sent. Without an API key,
        nothing is sent to an AI at all.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Memory is local and yours.</strong> What AGENCY learns about your usual choices stays on your
        Mac. You can see, change or erase any of it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No passwords, two-factor codes or card numbers.</strong> AGENCY never types, reads or stores
        them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Lifeline shares only what helpers need, only during an alert.</strong> Your name, what
        happened and your responder card go only to your own contacts, through personal links that stop
        showing the card when the alert ends.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Simulated by default.</strong> Out of the box, nobody real is contacted and nothing is bought.
        Real messages, calls and purchases need deliberate setup and your approval.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No telemetry.</strong> AGENCY OS doesn't report how you use it to anyone.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The full safety rules are in the project's <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/docs/os/PLAN.md`}>plan</a>,
      and Lifeline's in <a href={`${SOURCE_URL}/blob/main/LIFELINE.md`}>LIFELINE.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
    <p>
      <a class="btn" href={contact}>
        {CONTACT_EMAIL ? "Email us" : "Ask on GitHub"}
      </a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Last updated 10 October 2026. If this policy changes, the change will be visible in the site's public
      history on GitHub.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
